NEGRONI RAM (0401): XNU manages the whole DarwinBoot window (7 GiB from config/negroni-ne2211.toml [adt] --dram)
only after a self-check before arm_vm_init: window inside /chosen negroni-ram-bank, ADT dram-size/darwinboot-memory-size
= boot_args memSize, no overlap with /chosen negroni-ram-reserved (the GPU region) or with the GPU pool of the
boot-args (negronigpu_pool at negronigpu_poolbase). On a failure, or with the kill switch negroniram=0, XNU keeps
3072 MiB (the maxmem path), as before. One "NEGRONI RAM: on: ..." / "NEGRONI RAM: off: <reason> ..." line at EARLY_BOOT.
Host side: scripts/ios16/adt-extra.py (bank/reserved properties, Mu FD check, 3 GiB ADT fallback), patches/mu/0002,
docs/notes.md section 90.

